    "risk_summary": "Known V–Os superconductivity and B2/A15 order dependence are relevant references, but they do not identify this Os75V25 L12 phase. This source is configured noncollinear=false and SOC=false; a same-phase SOC effect and V spin response remain untested.",
    "ambient_scope": "Exact model force/full stress, converged electronic outputs, reported finite-q workflow and raw Γ optical evidence provide a bounded near-ambient source-model screen. Source residual stress/metastable alternatives remain explicit; this is not proof of synthesizeability, full BZ or global equilibrium.",
    "route_response": "Os-rich L12 A versus tetragonal B has all-ten λ improvement, all three separate fixed-μ Tc products favor A, and fine F lower for A by 19.26 meV/atom. Complete species-channel geometry differences and computed all-σ pairing response are saved against the frozen controls. Cell/grid/method sensitivity prevents a pure geometry-only causal claim; no bandwidth/carrier quantity is substituted.",
    "next_action": "Compare L12 and the explicit tetragonal control with the same spin/SOC and physical grids. An Os-SOC or competing-order response that reverses the source benefit is adverse; the historical V-rich alloy Tc cannot be assigned to A.",
